"The alley",
"The alley between the Quik-Stop and the church has had a name on city maps since 1931: Kestrel Mews. Nobody has ever called it that. People who work there at night do not have names either.",
"The alley is empty. Dex works nights. Obviously.",
"The apartment is small and the job is small and your life is small. It is yours, though. You keep it.",
"The back room",
"The back room. A desk, a beige computer, a safe older than Dee, and the hum of twenty machines through the wall.",
"The back says SWISS MADE in a font that has never been to Switzerland. Still, it ticks.",
"The bag is empty.",
"The bag is empty. She is washing your one pot with the energy of someone who has opinions about your sponge.",
"The ball goes over the fence. A kid on the other side throws it back without being asked.",
"The bench",
"The bench on Kestrel was donated \"in memory of Sal, who sat here.\" Sal is not dead. Sal sits there on Thursdays and finds the plaque very funny.",
"The bill: {0}. It will find you.",
"The block",
"The body keeps a ledger even when you do not: no sleep, no food, no water, a chemical schedule instead of a life. It calls in the debt all at once, in a stairwell, in front of a neighbour who will tell the story at parties for years.",
"The boiler at 1120 is being looked at. By me. I am looking at it.",
"The booker does not look up from the cash box. \"One a night. You had yours. Come back when the sun has been round.\"",
